pe":null},{"id":728,"title":"animation content","content":"<div><br><\/div><div><span style=\"color: rgb(75, 85, 99); font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, &quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;, &quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;; font-size: medium;\">At the school level, teaching animation sparks imagination, encourages self-expression, and develops critical 21st-century skills in students. Animation allows students to blend art, storytelling, and technology, enabling them to communicate complex ideas in a simple, creative form. The process of storyboarding, designing characters, and creating motion sequences builds essential skills such as problem-solving, attention to detail, and collaborative teamwork in students. Moreover, animation makes students resilient as they learn through trial and error, enhancing their ability to adapt and innovate. Through animation students not only develop digital fluency but also cultivate confidence in presenting their thoughts visually. It is an increasingly valuable skill in the modern, media-driven&nbsp;world.<\/span><\/div>","content_type":"text","image_path":null,"image_url":null,"link_url":null,"video_path":null,"video_url":null,"table_data":null,"accordion_data":null,"order":1,"is_active":true,"created_at":"2025-09-22T08:10:32.553000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T08:10:32.553000Z","page_section_id":"1820","content_heading":"animation content","alignment":null,"image_alt":null,"column_type":null,"width":"50","image_width":null,"image_height":null,"content_item_id":null,"content_item_type":null}]}]}}